   "evidence": "Hypothesis in diff: `(hF : \u2200 p\u2081 p\u2082 y, F p\u2082 p\u2081 y = F p\u2081 p\u2082 y)`; proof uses `MeasurableEquiv.prodCongr MeasurableEquiv.prodComm (MeasurableEquiv.refl T)`, i.e. `y` is held fixed. README \u00a76.1 lines 1110-1117 define the DPD with polarisation labels, for which the distribution depends on the direction of `y`.",
