   "fix": "Either state the restriction in the docstrings ('symmetric under exchange of the two partons at fixed `y`, the `y`-even case'), or generalise: take a measure-preserving involution `r : T \u2192 T` with `F p\u2082 p\u2081 (r y) = F p\u2081 p\u2082 y` (and likewise `F'`) and build the exchange equivalence as `prodCongr prodComm r`, so the theorem applies to the full \u00a76.1 DPD once it lands.",
   "issue": "`orderedDPSIntegral_comm` and `dpsCrossSection_eq_mul_orderedDPSIntegral` assume `F p\u2082 p\u2081 y = F p\u2081 p\u2082 y` at the same `y`, and the docstrings (and PR text, 'for any exchange-symmetric pair of DPDs') present this as the DPD exchange symmetry. The physical symmetry of the \u00a76.1 distribution is `F_{a\u2081a\u2082}(x\u2081,x\u2082,y) = F_{a\u2082a\u2081}(x\u2082,x\u2081,\u2212y)`; the stated hypothesis holds only for profiles even in `y` (unpolarised channels of an unpolarised hadron), and fails for the transversely polarised channels \u00a76.1 keeps. The pocket formula itself is unaffected (factorised `F` is trivially symmetric).",
   "line": 139
  }
